  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is continuous in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></msup></math> is continuous in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Thus, the number of points where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is discontinuous is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, the number of points where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is non-differentiable is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
